      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "57 patients with chest pain, had tomographic thallium-201 stress scintigraphy (TTSS), and coronary angiography within three months of the TTSS. The exercise images were compared with delayed images obtained at 3 hours post-exercise. The sensitivity and specificity of locating individual coronary artery disease was 88% and 100% for disease of left anterior descending artery (LAD), 89% and 83% for right coronary artery disease (RCA), and 24% and 96% for left circumflex artery (LCX) disease. Other than for LCX disease, our results compare favourably with other reports. The overall accuracies are 91%, 86% and 60% for LAD, RCA and LCX disease respectively."},
